    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** headlining the offensive core. **Gunnar Henderson** stands as our highest-scoring play at 74.74; despite facing the formidable Cole, his projections are heavily buoyed by a +16% park factor and the sustained upside of hitting in the three-hole. Similarly, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** benefits from a favorable matchup against Bradish, where his 73.66 score is driven by a strong platoon advantage and a premium spot in the order. **Sam Antonacci** and **Heliot Ramos** also present high-floor options; **Sam Antonacci** leverages a +17% boost from the matchup against Holmes, while **Heliot Ramos** remains a vital inclusion due to his speed upside and high-leverage lineup placement.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Nasim Nunez**, who finished just outside the starting threshold with a score of 37.99. While **Nasim Nunez** provides the elite stolen base profile we prioritize, the optimizer correctly flagged him as a liability today against the high-skill arm of deGrom, whose sub-3.20 xERA heavily penalized the base projection. With **Kyle Tucker**, **Luis Robert Jr.**, and **Jackson Merrill** all unavailable due to scheduled off-days, our bench depth is intentionally thin to preserve game caps. **Wade Meckler** remains the final start in the outfield at 48.71; while his score is marginally lower, his lead-off spot against Lambert provides enough volume to justify the start over speculative alternatives. We must monitor the official lineups for **Drake Baldwin** and **Miguel Vargas** closely, as any shift from their projected spots in the order could quickly compress their scores closer to the \"Below Floor\" category.",
